      "updated": 1788653831486,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Track causality explicitly instead of relying on wall-clock time. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Track causality explicitly instead of relying on wall-clock time. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RFE0eQWtusXfjl5IZVruU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 587.832885480585,
      "y": 3185.2246520424205,
      "width": 1043.2183837890625,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2004146965,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1178286567,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788653831486,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Example — Client writes key \"cart:42\":\n          Write 1 (via coordinator A): cart = [\"shoes\"]         VC: {A:1}\n          Write 2 (via coordinator A): cart = [\"shoes\",\"socks\"]  VC: {A:2}     ← causally AFTER write 1 (A:2 descends A:1)\n  Network partition. Two clients write concurrently to DIFFERENT coordinators:\n          Write 3 (via coordinator A): cart = [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"hat\"]   VC: {A:3}\n          Write 4 (via coordinator B): cart = [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"gloves\"] VC: {A:2, B:1}\n\n  Neither VC descends the other → CONCURRENT, not causally ordered\n          → get(\"cart:42\") returns BOTH as \"siblings\":\n               [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"hat\"]    {A:3}\n               [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"gloves\"] {A:2,B:1}\n          → Client (or app logic) merges: [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"hat\",\"gloves\"]\n          → Resolved write carries a VC descending BOTH parents: {A:4, B:1}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Example — Client writes key \"cart:42\":\n          Write 1 (via coordinator A): cart = [\"shoes\"]         VC: {A:1}\n          Write 2 (via coordinator A): cart = [\"shoes\",\"socks\"]  VC: {A:2}     ← causally AFTER write 1 (A:2 descends A:1)\n  Network partition. Two clients write concurrently to DIFFERENT coordinators:\n          Write 3 (via coordinator A): cart = [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"hat\"]   VC: {A:3}\n          Write 4 (via coordinator B): cart = [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"gloves\"] VC: {A:2, B:1}\n\n  Neither VC descends the other → CONCURRENT, not causally ordered\n          → get(\"cart:42\") returns BOTH as \"siblings\":\n               [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"hat\"]    {A:3}\n               [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"gloves\"] {A:2,B:1}\n          → Client (or app logic) merges: [\"shoes\",\"socks\",\"hat\",\"gloves\"]\n          → Resolved write carries a VC descending BOTH parents: {A:4, B:1}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
